Chapter Ten — “The Land of the Lion King”

Chapter 10, Part 35 — “The White Ram”

With a thud, Subaru’s head hit the floor.

Seeing the utterly unrestrained way his head had fallen, Felix instinctively thought—

This is bad.

“――――”

Whether at the clinic or on battlefields he had been dispatched to as part of his duties, Felix had seen more wounds and blood than he cared to remember. So he knew.

Someone who had suffered a truly critical injury could no longer even manage the actions necessary to protect themselves.

Just like Subaru now, they could do nothing but collapse onto the floor, unable even to shield their head.

“――――!”

Slowly, blood began to seep from Subaru’s right flank, flowing out and spreading across the landing.

Whenever Felix saw blood, he always thought the same thing.

――It was as though someone’s life itself were flowing out.

“Hey, something about this is awfully strange. Red and white are such a wonderful combination, and I always think they look absolutely gorgeous together, but… more importantly, you! Why did you do something like that? Could it be… jealousy? Which means――love!?”

It was difficult to believe that Bellaris was looking at the same scene.

After commenting on the blood flowing from the fallen Subaru and the whiteness of the floor, Bellaris extended both hands toward the woman――toward the “White Ram.”

The White Ram, who had stabbed Subaru from behind and now wore an utterly cold expression.

She quietly returned Bellaris's gaze while wiping her bloodstained fingers with a handkerchief.

“――――!”

“I suppose so. It’s love. In the end, that’s the motive behind everything we do, isn’t it?”

“An affirmation!? So it really is that! Natsuki is head-over-heels for Felix, and you couldn’t stand it, so you stabbed him! Oh, how terrible, what a tragedy! You, driven mad by jealousy, and Felix, crying out as he stares love straight in the face… Who am I supposed to root for!?”

The difference in temperature between the White Ram and Bellaris's responses was incredible.

Yet Felix, who was not taking either side, was irritated by the sheer absurdity of Bellaris's words.

To claim that Felix was crying out was an utterly warped interpretation of the situation.

He wasn't crying out.

He was simply――

“――Subaru-kun! No! Don't die! Come over here… come over here!”

――simply calling out to someone who was dying, as a healer, even if only barely qualified as one.

“What a tragedy.”

He shook his body and strained his arms, desperately trying to get to Subaru.

But Felix's body, pinned against the wall, would not budge even an inch.

Meanwhile, Bellaris walked toward the center of the landing, her footsteps echoing.

――Right between Felix and the White Ram.

There, she extended both hands toward the two of them.

“On one side, the person who was chased after overcoming the ‘detour’ through sheer blood, sweat, and tears. On the other, the person who could do nothing but cling to that desperate back from the closest position possible. And that sinful Natsuki is going to leave the two of you behind and pass away… This is it!”

“――This is what?”

“Love burns hotter when the obstacles are higher, doesn't it? Age and gender are both kindling that stokes love. But then, what is the greatest obstacle of all? It is――separation!”

“――――”

“Separation by death! That is love's greatest obstacle! Because once someone dies, it’s over! You can never touch someone who has died again. So there’s nothing that can drive two people farther apart than death, right? Which means, conversely, death is the medicine that heightens the love between two people who love each other to its absolute limit! Death is an aphrodisiac!”

She was insane.

Bellaris spoke with a blissful smile and ecstatic eyes. There was no question that something was wrong with her head.

How much the White Ram agreed with that deranged theory of love, Felix couldn't tell.

But rather than laugh at Bellaris's ravings or disparage them――

“――Mama, thank you for everything. I love you more than anyone in the world.”

It was an abrupt statement, completely unrelated to anything that had been said, and one that made no sense.

At least to Felix, it seemed that, just as with Subaru before he had been stabbed, the White Ram's mental imbalance had been caused by the “poison” Bellaris had been spreading around.

But――

“――――”

Bellaris's reaction was completely different.

The color drained from her face in an instant, leaving her deathly pale.

Seeing Bellaris like that, something changed in the White Ram's cold expression.

A smile.

A derisive smile utterly unsuited to her features appeared on her face.

“――I am an ‘Beloved Child’ sent into the ‘Six Tongues’ by Mama.”

“――Ah.”

“I infiltrated them to grasp the full picture of the ‘Six Tongues’ and strip our enemies completely bare. But if things continued like this, it looked as though the ‘Beloved Children’ were going to end up fighting one another, so I decided to reveal myself.

――Please consider this a little gift. She was surprisingly troublesome. If she were acting normally.”

“This,” she said, kicking Subaru's body, lying face-down in the pool of blood, with the tip of her toe.

At that callous treatment of Subaru, Bellaris, who had been frozen stiff, slowly――deeply――exhaled.

It was not the sigh of a woman seeing a nightmare that had been her breath until now.

It was one of profound, profound relief.

“Ah, ah, I see. So that's how it is. You're a ‘Beloved Child’ too… You're not Mama herself, right? If that's the case, then thank goodness. See, Mama does that sometimes, doesn't she? She wants to understand us from the bottom of our hearts, so once there was a day when every single person I met was Mama! I thought my heart was going to freeze when I remembered it… You're not Mama, right?”

“Yes. I am myself. But I understand how you feel. I've had things done to me many times that made it difficult to get food down my throat, too.”

“You too! We're the same, aren't we… Is that why you confided in me? Does that mean it's fate? You don't want to lose me? Me neither!”

At the feet of the two “Beloved Children” chatting amicably, the blood of a pitiful boy who had been abandoned by love continued to flow.

Little by little, but surely, it was shaving away his life.

With every passing second, the possibility of gathering up the life spilling away from him disappeared.

“And yet, what are you two taking your time for…? Me too…!”

She hated it.

She was angry.

She was irritated.

She was furious at the “Beloved Children” who had prepared this hourglass of blood, and at herself for being able to do nothing but watch.

More than that, she was even furious at Subaru, who had barged in here so carelessly only to be neatly stabbed by a traitor.

It had been like this for the entire past two months.

She had been angry with Subaru to the point of being unable to stand it.

――Why had Subaru left Emilia's side?

Why had he once again left the person he should have remained closest to, trying instead to reach out a hand to Crusch in her moment of crisis?

And now he had separated himself from both his master and his companions, lying in a pool of blood.

It was completely backwards.

Natsuki Subaru's actions――his very existence――were the embodiment of Felix Argyle's sins.

If, because of his weakness, things had been taken from him and he could only ask those around him to compensate for the fate that had befallen him, then having Subaru make up for those deficiencies was entirely Felix's sin.

――And Felix's sins always ended up being paid for by someone other than himself.

“Don't mess with me…”

Once, Felix's birth had destroyed the Argyle family――the beast-like ears that appeared as a manifestation of his demi-human blood's reversion to an ancestral trait had caused his father to suspect his mother of infidelity.

Once, Felix's arrogance had caused him to miss his opportunity to repay his mentor.

――That deeply beneficent mentor, who had affirmed this power of his, had his judgment called into question, and his life was taken by someone driven beyond reason.

Once, Felix's negligence had prevented him from saving the close friend he genuinely revered.

――Despite being praised as “Blue,” he had failed to save his lord's beloved because his abilities had fallen short of his reputation.

Once, Felix's atonement had failed to reach the master he valued more dearly than his own life――twice.

――And even now, his own inadequacy was threatening to bring about a third betrayal of his master.

“That's not funny… It's not funny…!”

He twisted his body.

His arms would not come free.

He put strength into his shoulders.

His arms would not tear loose.

He kicked the wall with all his might.

His arms remained trapped.

Nothing――not a single thing――would go the way Felix wanted.

Just like Felix's life.

“――!”

His directionless anger rampaged within his hateful, painfully thin chest.

He could keep his body in perfect condition, but he couldn't keep his heart that way.

In fact, had there ever been a time when his heart was in perfect condition?

Always emotionally unstable, always making a racket with his fragile heart.

Because he was like that, he had been unable to save a single person――

“――Ah.”

Once again, he was being punished.

He had ruined someone else's life.

――And as he clenched his teeth, cursing the fate that had become entangled with Felix's life――

“――――”

Subaru's black eyes met his.

Subaru lay face-down in the pool of blood, his face turned to the side.

His arms and legs were sprawled carelessly, his eyes unfocused, his breathing shallow and weak, bubbles of blood frothing between his lips.

The face of someone standing on the brink of death.

It was a face Felix had seen countless times before.

There was only one difference.

Only one point that separated Subaru from those who were captured by death and taken away.

Those who were being taken away died with grief, fear, and regret in their eyes.

But Subaru was different.

In those powerless, unfocused black eyes, there was hope.

――The moment Felix understood what that hope was directed toward, he realized.

The terribly foolish act of relying on someone else that the weak, fragile, powerless Natsuki Subaru had just played.

“Don't mess with me…!”

What spilled from Felix's mouth next was different from the directionless anger of moments before.

This was a viscous crystallization of the curse-like anger within Felix, directed straight at the person it ought to be directed toward.

Even now, at this very moment, Natsuki Subaru still believed in Felix Argyle.

――This entire thing was an absurdly stupid little performance, staged on nothing but that hope.

　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　△▼△▼△▼△

――We go back to before Subaru and the “White Ram” descended underground.

“I'll choose, too.

――So that I can face that person without shame.”

In response to the White Ram's decision, Subaru decided that their route should be underground.

Their policy was to avoid the safety-first approach of slamming on the brakes, but that didn't mean he intended to equate it with recklessness.

Relying on Cor Leonis to locate Felix, while leaving the route's corrections to the White Ram's instructions, the two advanced toward their destination at the highest speed they could manage without rushing recklessly.

But even if they reached their destination like this, without any means of doing anything, it would be meaningless.

“Isn't something weird about this in the first place? Why is the enemy keeping Felix alive?”

While concentrating his consciousness on his Authority during the journey, Subaru was also focused on increasing the number of cards in his hand.

In most cases, useful cards were sleeping among the garbage cards.

And even without deliberately trying to collect them, countless garbage cards had accumulated throughout the two months of wandering blindly in the dark.

Not merely since arriving at this castle.

Even throughout the countless days of searching blindly over the past two months.

“‘They're following Capella's policy and trying not to kill as much as possible’ is rejected on the grounds that, if nothing else, it'd be pretty damn unfortunate for my life. So I can think of two possibilities.”

One was that Felix's healing ability was far beyond what the enemy had imagined, and that they had actually thought they had finished him off, leaving the mortally wounded Felix abandoned somewhere underground.

And the other was――

“――The enemy has a reason for wanting to keep Felix alive.”

“They want information from him, or they intend to use him as a hostage…?”

“That's the most plausible explanation. But taking into account my pitiful wealth of experience, there's one incredibly unpleasant possibility that comes to mind.

――Capella wants to adopt Felix, too.”

When Subaru had been told that the “Beloved Children” were a collection of people with talents specialized in a single field, he had thought Felix was practically tailor-made for the group.

Of course, trying to analyze Capella's warped concept of love was an exercise in futility, so this was nothing more than a conjecture based on the current circumstances.

“…That might be possible. No, actually, that's probably the explanation that makes the most sense.”

“It's reassuring if even you think it's possible, ‘White Ram’-chan. Honestly, when I thought it was a shitty idea… I got freaked out when I realized I'd done the same thing, turning someone I'd captured into one of my own kids.”

“Huh? Wha—what? Whaaaa!?”

The White Ram was stunned by Subaru's self-reflection, but the details would only be noise, so he left them out.

Obviously, he was talking about Meili.

He would insist that there was a fundamental difference between his educational philosophy and Capella's.

――There were also things he wanted to discuss with Meili about this matter, but those could wait.

“Anyway, if this possibility is correct, then, weirdly enough, maybe we don't have to worry about Felix being killed. But even in that case, I still want to reunite with him.”

“…May I ask why?”

“Two reasons. The first is the same as before we set out: if Felix is around, our survival rate goes through the roof. The second is the enemy's abilities. I want to deal with the most dangerous one――‘Lost Child.’”

The White Ram drew a small breath, and Subaru nodded as he continued walking, tracing the wall with one hand.

At present, the three “Beloved Children” known to have appeared in Kugelschreiber Castle were “Silence,” “Rupture,” and “Lost Child.”

Subaru believed the last of them was the most difficult enemy.

Of course, the assassination ability of “Silence” and the troublesome nature of “Rupture” went without saying.

“If we're already fighting ‘Silence,’ then Crusch-san has a way to counter her. And for ‘Rupture,’ I've thought of a way to deal with it. But ‘Lost Child’ is different. As long as that's around, we'll never be able to reunite with our allies.”

The reason Subaru could attempt to reunite with Felix now was that two conditions had been satisfied: the effect of Cor Leonis, and the fact that Felix himself had not moved from his position.

The most terrifying thing about “Lost Child” was that the moment its target started moving, the difficulty of reuniting with them skyrocketed.

“So we've got to disable ‘Lost Child.’ And for that, Felix's――”

“W-wait a second! I'm being completely left behind here! You can actually do something about that ability that makes everyone's emotions go haywire!?”

“Yeah. I think I can. I can't say one hundred percent, and it pisses me off that it means relying on that piece-of-shit Regulus's power, but we've already confirmed that an Authority ranks above ‘Lost Child.’”

The White Ram fell silent.

Feeling her stare fixed intently on him, Subaru opened his eyes.

While they had been considering the matter, they had arrived just short of where Felix was.

They needed to talk here.

The plan Subaru had come up with absolutely required the White Ram's cooperation.

“――‘White Ram’-chan, there's something I'd like to ask you to hear out. Whether we can pull it off depends on you, so I want your opinion.”

“A plan? And one that depends on me…?”

“As you know, if there's an enemy waiting ahead, there's a pretty good chance the two of us won't be able to deal with them head-on. So here, I want to play dirty and launch a surprise attack.”

“Surprise attack…”

The White Ram stopped alongside Subaru, prompting him to continue.

“Tell me. What do you want me to do?”

“Simple. ‘White Ram’-chan is a spy sent by Capella into the ‘Six Tongues.’ You catch me while I was trying to launch a sneak attack on them, and then you bring me in to join the ‘Beloved Children’… Something like that.”

“――! That…”

“I told you, right? The ‘Beloved Children’ barely know each other. But ‘White Ram’-chan actually used to be one of the ‘Beloved Children,’ so you've got something in common with them.

If you show up with me as a little gift, don't you think we'd have a better chance than going in head-on?”

It must have been far more unexpected than she had anticipated.

The White Ram covered her mouth with both hands, eyes opened wide.

Of course, it wasn't nearly as easy as Subaru made it sound, and there was no way the enemy would believe it without question.

But throughout the “Beloved Children” front over the past two months, Subaru had repeatedly seen that the enemy shared surprisingly little information with one another, each struggling to fulfill Capella's wishes within the scope of their assigned abilities and authority.

Capella's dictatorship as their leader, their lack of thorough cooperation even among allies because of their disciplinary structure, and their false loyalty bound together by fear――

Subaru suspected there might be openings to exploit.

There was one problem.

This plan required the “White Ram” herself to be prepared to confront that fear once again.

“I think… there is a chance. Maybe, for reasons that ‘Ash Star’-san doesn't know, things could go better than you expect.”

“Seriously? I'm curious about those reasons, but if they're a positive factor, I'll gladly take them.”

“But we might stumble right at the beginning. Even if I take ‘Ash Star’-san with me, there's no guarantee they'll believe me…”

“――Then what if we could create a situation where they had no choice but to believe us?”

The White Ram's objection was exactly what Subaru had expected, and he agreed with it.

Even if the White Ram brought Subaru in with his hands tied behind his back, there was a good chance they would realize she was making a desperate gamble.

That's why his proposal had been prepared in two stages.

Though it would place a heavy burden on the White Ram.

Because――

“…‘White Ram’-chan, are you carrying any weapons?”

“Weapons…? I have a collapsible staff for martial arts, and a dagger, just in case. Do you need them?”

“Yeah, I need you to use one. …For impact, the knife, right…”

She showed him the two weapons hidden on her person: a baton-length staff and a dagger shaped somewhat like a survival knife.

Subaru decided the latter was better suited to his purpose.

Then, looking at the White Ram's confused expression as he made a bitter face, he told her:

“――If we run into a ‘Beloved Child,’ stab me with that knife. If we go that far, we'd add a hell of a lot more credibility to the story, wouldn't we?”

　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　△▼△▼△▼△

“If we don't have enough credibility, then we add credibility. I considered the pattern where you beat me to within an inch of my life, too, but that won't fool Todd. You know, because he's cautious and suspicious.”

“――――”

“If we underestimate the enemy and only go halfway, we won't get the result we want. If we're doing this, we bet everything on one point and throw ourselves into it completely.”

“W-wait…”

“I'll give the performance of a lifetime, too. I'll make it look completely convincing when you do it to me. But without a doubt, the burden will be heavier on you, ‘White Ram’-chan, so whether you can――”

“――Please, wait!”

The mouth rapidly explaining the plan was silenced by her shout.

The White Ram raised her voice, pressed the hand she had held against her mouth to her chest, and felt the pounding of her heart beneath her palm as she looked at Subaru with tear-filled eyes.

――As expected, it was too much.

Subaru had already understood that the White Ram was gentle and disliked conflict.

Even if this was all part of a plan, telling her to stab him was cruel beyond measure――

“…That's not what you really want, Subaru-san.”

“…‘White Ram’-chan?”

“Putting yourself in danger like that just to increase the chances that I can succeed――that's not what you really want.

…I'm the one who made you say it.”

The White Ram gripped the front of her clothing tightly, drawing in her thin shoulders as her voice trembled.

But Subaru didn't understand what she meant.

Even if she said that he had made her say it, he had no idea what she was talking about.

It was Subaru, unmistakably, who had come up with the plan.

Still, trying to calm her as she shrank into herself, he reached a hand toward her shoulder.

“I don't really understand what you're saying. Maybe you're confused from the shock――”

“――! Don't touch me!”

“――!”

The hand he had tried to extend was slapped away, and Subaru involuntarily caught his breath.

For an instant, even the White Ram's cheeks stiffened at her own overreaction.

But she quickly pressed her lips together.

“Don't touch me. If you do, Subaru-san will surely become even more…”

“More? More what? ‘White Ram’-chan, I don't understand. We don't have time to stand around right now. Please, just tell me clearly!”

“More obedient to me! That's my power!”

The White Ram raised her voice even louder than Subaru had.

She held out both hands.

The hands on either side, with their slender, supple fingers, were shown clearly to Subaru as she said――

“My power is ‘Bewitching.’ It makes anyone I touch with these hands develop affection for me. And once someone has feelings for me, they become unable to refuse my requests…”

“‘White Ram’-chan's requests…”

“Doesn't anything come to mind? When I held your hand and talked to you, didn't you sometimes feel, somehow, that what I was saying was right, and end up agreeing with me?”

Hearing that, Subaru lowered his eyes and recalled the two months since he had met the White Ram.

It was true.

There might have been several moments like that.

When he had been unsure or unable to decide, there had been times when the White Ram touched him and he simply went along with the proposal she made.

“But that was…”

“――I don't like this power. I hate it. Because I feel like I'm trampling over everyone around me, using all of them for my own sake.”

“――――”

“So normally, I tried to stay as far away from Subaru-san and Beatrice-san as possible. I was careful not to accidentally touch you…”

That earnest effort was surely genuine.

She had avoided physical contact with others as much as she could.

And even on the rare occasions when she did take Subaru's hand――

“Russell's orders, huh? So it wasn't just because ‘White Ram’-chan used to be a ‘Beloved Child.’ She was incredibly useful because she had this power too.

When you put it that way, it makes sense.”

No wonder Russell had counted the White Ram――who was obviously unsuited to the role in terms of personality――as one of the principal weapons in the fight against the “Six Tongues.”

In other words, she was a honey trap artist who didn't need seduction, with an almost guaranteed success rate.

“So this plan just now was also the result of me being bewitched by ‘White Ram’-chan.”

“――. Yes.”

The White Ram nodded solemnly.

She looked like a sinner who had confessed her crime, remorseful over the sin she had committed.

In truth, that was probably exactly how she felt.

She had been born with the ability to draw affection out of others and use it to bring about results convenient for herself.

She was tormented by the awareness that she had been indulging in every conceivable kind of vice.

And now, when Subaru had proposed a plan that involved hurting himself, all the guilt she had been carrying had exploded.

The influence of “Rupture,” which made it difficult to contain one's emotions, probably played no small part as well.

If that was the case, then Subaru was probably being affected by “Rupture,” too.

――Otherwise, there was absolutely no way Subaru would say something like this to the White Ram.

“‘White Ram’-chan.”

“I'm sorry, but please reconsider. That plan is far too reckless. I'm unharmed, yet it's a plan where you might die…”

“――I've got a girl I like very much, so I'm not going to die for you, ‘White Ram’-chan.”

“――. ――――. ―――――What?”

At Subaru's declaration, the White Ram, who had been wearing the face of a guilty sinner, stared at him in stunned disbelief.

Her eyes widened.

Subaru felt bad for leaving her unable to argue, but time was precious.

He continued while he had the chance.

He had to correct the misunderstanding the White Ram had.

“You're a pretty gorgeous girl yourself, ‘White Ram’-chan, but to me, that girl is the brightest star in the sky. Her radiance looks different from everyone else's.

So I haven't been bewitched by you.”

“――――”

“And there's one other misunderstanding… Well, that's partly because I explained it badly. I said whether we can pull this off depends on you, right?

But you're not the person I'm relying on for this plan.”

“Th-then, who…?”

Subaru sincerely regretted putting her through unnecessary emotional distress.

He had done something terrible to her.

――To begin with, Subaru and the White Ram had fundamentally different assumptions regarding the risk involved.

The White Ram thought the plan carried the risk that Subaru might die.

But Subaru was different.

This was a plan in which Subaru might suffer enough pain to feel like he was going to die.

But he wouldn't actually die.

Because――

“――Felix. I'm relying on him.”

“Ah…”

“He said it himself. If someone is in front of him, even if they want to die, he won't let them die.

That's why this plan only works if we do it right in front of him.”

In exchange, if they caused the incident in front of Felix, he would keep that promise out of sheer stubborn pride.

Because Subaru respected that kind strength of his――the gentle strength of someone who, in only two months, had rewritten the principles of healing magic so that even a spirit could be saved, all because of the possibility that something might happen to Beatrice.

Relying on Felix was the same kind of desperate reliance on others as relying on Reinhard or Julius.

――That was the core of this “Natsuki Subaru Fake Murder Case.”

“Also, I just said I wasn't bewitched, but I think we've gotten pretty close. But that's not only because of your power. You check on me when things are rough, you take the initiative to make tea during breaks, and, well, I'm just really easy to win over.”

“Subaru-san…”

“I don't think you cheated or tricked me.

We're comrades. Let's help each other.

It's a much better proposal than having Felix suddenly watch me get stabbed right in front of him, isn't it?”

Saying that, Subaru deliberately held out his right hand and invited the White Ram to shake it.

The White Ram looked down at the offered hand and swallowed hard.

“…I can't believe in people's kindness.

Even what Subaru-san just said――I can't help thinking that, in the end, my power made you say it.

That's what I think about that person, too.”

“――――”

“But… but today, I'll try believing.

I'll believe in you――the person who tells me that you can trust someone other than yourself, trust them more than you trust yourself.”

Tentatively, her hand reached out and touched Subaru's.

Then she clasped it firmly.

That handshake was proof that a girl who feared manipulating the hearts of those she touched had taken a courageous step forward.

And the way she would use that courage was to stab Subaru.

“Well, that's quite the conclusion, but… think you can do it, ‘White Ram’-chan?”

“Melty.”

“Huh?”

“――Melty Pristis.

That's my name.”

Subaru's eyes widened.

The “White Ram”――no, Melty Pristis――softened her lips into a smile.

It was the face of a girl who, despite carrying cowardice within her heart, had decided to resist with whatever courage she could muster.

After surprising Subaru with that smile and introduction, she squeezed the hand they had clasped together and said――

“This is my first time making a friend.

And it's also my first time stabbing a friend!”

It was an incredibly gallant declaration from a new friend.

And with that, the “Natsuki Subaru Fake Murder Case” was set into motion――

