“――Gah, guh――”

Thus, Subaru was actually stabbed for the sake of the surprise attack, leaving him in critical condition.

By specifying the right flank, he had barely reduced the risk of bleeding to death, but the difference was negligible.

He had no strength left in his body and couldn't move.

Lying in a pool of blood, he felt as though he might drown in his own blood.

But he couldn't die.

If he died, it would mean committing an offense against the White Ram――no, Melty――who had trusted Subaru and carried out the plan.

An offense he could never atone for, even in death.

“So don't die, damn it…!”

With everything he had, Subaru held on to the life that was already beginning to slip away from his body.

Repeating shallow breaths, he forced his entire aching body to tense up, not only the flank where the knife was embedded.

He had another role to fulfill.

The role of the gift who had been stabbed and left dying――and the role of suppressing the damage caused by “Rupture.”

“Cor… Leo…nis…”

Along with the hoarse whisper, the “Greed” Authority――Cor Leonis was abused once more.

He didn't need to say the name to use it, but right now he wanted to keep his head working even a little.

If he relaxed his focus, his consciousness might disappear in the next instant and he might die.

Even the agony of abusing the Authority was welcome if it meant providing some kind of change.

Within that change, Subaru sensed the presence of his scattered companions throughout Kugelschreiber Castle.

Each one was a source of strength that kept Subaru connected to the world.

But locating his companions was not the true purpose behind activating Cor Leonis.

――It was the restoration of the “Little King.”

And when that was accomplished, the emotions of “two people” came crashing into Subaru as a “Rupture.”

“Ugh, guh, ugh, aahhh… That's too much…!”

An overwhelmingly powerful wave of emotion.

A raging storm.

The collapse of the dam within his heart caused by it made Subaru, on the brink of death, whine in misery, topping the pool of blood with tears and snot.

A disgusting three-minute cooking show.

The sensation was so intense, so violent, and so much stronger than anywhere else in the castle that Subaru understood perfectly well that the source of “Rupture” was this shipper-obsessed ghost woman.

He understood.

He really, really understood.

“――I've made my choice. I, too, am choosing in order to make my wish come true.”

Melty's performance as she said that and stabbed Subaru in the flank was nothing short of spectacular.

She was unquestionably a leading candidate for an Academy Award.

As expected, a woman with the courage to leave the “Beloved Children” was on another level.

And just as expected, she approached the shipper-obsessed ghost who had taken control of this place――

“My name is Melty. May I ask your name?”

“My name? My name is Bellaris. They call me the ‘Ring Finger.’

Oh, but this is terrible! The fact that we've introduced ourselves means our story has already begun… Wait, I might like you. I think I might love you, Melty!”

“Don't say ‘might.’ That's such a lonely thing to say.

Aren't we family?”

With a slightly sulky tone, Melty raised her hand and gently placed it against the shipper――Bellaris's――cheek.

At once, Bellaris's cheeks flushed.

“Ah.”

Her eyes became moist with heat.

If Melty's power really was what she had claimed, then this was her true ability, now that she had thrown away her inhibitions――she had been right when she said she might be able to do this far better than Subaru expected.

“Bellaris, are you here on Mama's orders?”

“No, Dandon told me to come. Well, strictly speaking, Dandon told me to wait.

But Reborn ignored him… Reborn must want Dandon's attention, right!?”

“Bellaris, how did you find out about this place?”

“Apparently there was a report from the ‘Executor.’

I don't know the details of how he found out, but that's mysterious too, which makes it wonderful, doesn't it? Whose eyes is he looking into…? Me?”

“Bellaris, who else is here besides you?”

“Reborn and Tornel.

Originally, Reborn was only going to bring Tornel, but you can't let two people go on a secret rendezvous alone, can you? So I forced my way into coming along.

My ‘Ring Finger’ gets along with anyone, so…

Ah, don't think I'm promiscuous! I just want to spread lots of love, and I want to see people giving love to each other, too…!”

Bellaris took Melty's hand herself and clung to her as she pleaded.

From her mouth flowed, without end, the previously unspoken circumstances of the “Beloved Children” who had invaded the castle.

Of course, some of it was probably due to Bellaris being careless by nature.

But more than that, what loosened her tongue was the terrifying power of “Bewitching”――used from the outset while making the target believe she was an ally.

You probably couldn't cheat on someone with this.

They'd find out immediately.

She'd make you confess.

It was unmistakably proof that Melty Pristis had once been one of the “Beloved Children.”

“――――”

For just an instant, Melty's gaze crossed with Subaru's as he lay collapsed on the floor.

He could barely nod, give a thumbs-up, or even signal with his eyes, but he had witnessed the reliability of her power.

It had been worth taking on the burden of “Rupture” for her.

All that remained was――

“Bellaris, actually, there's another ‘Beloved Child’ with me.

But we've gotten lost inside the castle and can't reunite, and it's causing us trouble.”

“What!? You mean you can't meet someone you want to see? That's such a tragedy…

Though I think love grows bigger the longer people keep missing each other…”

“――But that would cause trouble for Mama.”

“――――”

No matter how dramatic an effect those words had, Felix was certain he could never, for the rest of his life, bring himself to welcome the fear and terror that appeared on Bellaris's profile at that moment.

“Tornel! Undo the ‘Detour’! Those two who can't meet each other are pitiful!”

Bellaris shouted that into the underground passageways, unable to completely hide the tremor in her voice.

At that moment, there was a single click.

Blue light spread through the underground.

It traced over Subaru, Melty and Bellaris, Felix against the wall, and then spread farther outward――probably throughout the entire castle.

And as the light faded and its afterglow receded, Subaru instinctively understood.

“Yes! The ‘Detour’ is gone now. You should be able to meet the person you want to meet properly.

But if you don't mind, I'd like you to reunite in front of me. It's so exciting!”

As though confirming that intuition, Bellaris――who was rubbing her cheek against Melty's hand――declared it.

And with that, one objective of the “Natsuki Subaru Fake Murder Case” had been accomplished.

With the “Detour”解除――with the “Detour” undone――now everyone who had been separated could safely――

――meet――

“――Don't die, idiot!! What the hell were you thinking!? Don't mess around!!”

――At that instant, the back of Subaru's dying consciousness was grabbed and he was forcibly dragged back into reality.

“――Ah.”

“Idiot! You were about to die just now, weren't you!? I can't believe you, I can't believe you, I can't believe you!

Why would you do something that stupid!? Why…!?”

He could hear a voice trembling with tears.

A voice lamenting and screaming, asking why, why.

There was no way he could leave her crying like that.

That was why he had to cling to his life by the narrowest possible margin.

“――――”

Instead of responding, Subaru caught something at the edge of his vision.

Countless slashes appeared across the ceiling.

Beyond the white canopy that had been cut open, a shadow came diving down into the underground――

